<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samuel Pepys</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1633–1703</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samuel Pepys was an English naval administrator and member of parliament, best known for the diary he kept from 1660 to 1669, describing the Restoration court, the Great Plague and the Great Fire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. As Secretary to the Admiralty he helped reform the navy. He was treasurer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> committee and went with the expedition that evacuated English Tangier in 1683–1684.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-pepys.jpg" alt="Samuel Pepys" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Hayls · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samuel_Pepys.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
